==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|sa|en}} {{m|sa|नमस्कार}}, from {{m|sa|नमस्||bow, [[obeisance]]}} and {{m|sa|कार||action}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/naməˈskɑː/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{label|en|India}} The use of the [[greet]]ing in which you put your hands together and then [[bow]] slightly; greeting with a [[namaste]]. {{defdate|from 19th c.}}
#* '''1997''', {{w|Kiran Nagarkar}}, ''Cuckold'', HarperCollins 2013, p. 228:
#*: I bowed down, did '''namaskar''' and said a prayer.

